WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.120
hey everyone, it's professor Dave, I want to tell you some things about ozonolysis.

00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:15.020
ozonolysis is a reaction that utilizes ozone as a reagent

00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:20.540
ozone is a triatomic allotrope of oxygen that exists as a zwitterion

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:23.620
that's ozone, that's the stuff up in the atmosphere

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:33.180
ozonolysis utilizes an alkene substrate and what happens is that this double bond

00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:39.440
gets cleaved and pulled apart, and each of the carbons that was participating in the double bond

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:42.600
is now a carbonyl.

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:48.900
so this is useful for transforming alkenes into ketones and aldehydes.

00:00:49.512 --> 00:00:55.912
we won't look at the mechanism here, but that is available on the internet for you to take a look at

00:00:55.912 --> 00:00:58.083
it's a little bit interesting to look at

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:05.440
the reason this is a very useful reaction is that we can do some things like transforming

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:11.640
terminal alkenes into aldehydes which is something that can be very useful for synthesis

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:16.960
so basically any time you are looking at an ozonolysis reaction, remember that we are cleaving

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:22.300
that double bond and pulling apart the fragments and on each of the carbons that was participating

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:27.360
in the double bond, we will place an oxygen atom, and it will be in the form of a carbonyl

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:30.900
here we are generating this aldehyde and formaldehyde

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:36.260
which can easily be separated, we've changed the functionality of a part of this molecule

00:01:36.260 --> 00:01:38.660
which may be useful for the next step in a synthesis

00:01:40.580 --> 00:01:45.620
the other thing that's interesting about ozonolysis is if you perform ozonolysis on a cyclic alkene

00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:52.280
you won't then get two molecules, you will simply pull apart that ring and get one linear product

00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:58.900
this is useful to number sometimes when we have cyclic structures like this

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:02.840
we want to take these seven carbons

00:02:05.771 --> 00:02:10.813
it's very easy to draw an incorrect product if we don't do something like numbering the carbons

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:17.780
what this is going to do for us is show that if we cleave this double bond and pull that molecule apart 

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:25.673
we know that the resulting carbonyls when we draw the linear product must be on carbons 2 and 7

00:02:25.673 --> 00:02:29.806
because those were the carbons that were participating in the double bond

00:02:29.806 --> 00:02:33.006
that's just a trick to help you draw the correct ozonolysis product.

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:36.678
thanks for watching, guys. subscribe to my channel for more tutorials

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:39.340
and as always feel free to email me with questions 

